  "text": "In the present study, one of the most significant findings was that the knowledge about CKD had no relation to income, where Participants with the highest income had the lowest knowledge levels 51.2%, we think that this may be attributed to the better healthcare access and screening among well-off population, on the contrary the Saudi study [14] found a link between higher levels of knowledge and higher economic position. Furthermore, our study suggested a positive correlation between the adequate level of knowledge among southern residents in Riyadh 63.4%, this might be related to the presence of Al Iman General Hospital and its health awareness activities in that area. In comparison, Assiry et al. [14] reported that only 27.3% of their 440 respondents in Jazan Province demonstrated good knowledge of CKD, with high awareness of risk factors and of complications in merely 7.5% and 9.3% of participants respectively, which is markedly lower than the 63.4% adequate knowledge observed among our southern Riyadh residents and further supports the presence of regional disparities in CKD awareness within Saudi Arabia."
}

