  "text": "CKD is a growing global health concern that significantly affects morbidity and mortality rates worldwide [3]. The prevalence of CKD has steadily increased over the past few decades due to the rising incidence of risk factors such as diabetes, hypertension, and obesity [4]. In Saudi Arabia, CKD poses a particular challenge, with the country witnessing a steady rise in the number of patients suffering from end-stage renal disease (ESRD) [5]. Despite the severity of CKD and its associated complications, public awareness regarding the disease, especially in non-medical populations, remains insufficient . Studies have shown that early detection and lifestyle modifications can significantly delay the progression of CKD and improve patient outcomes . However, limited research has been conducted on the awareness and knowledge of CKD among young adults, particularly among university students who are not pursuing medical degrees [7][8]."
