  "text": "This study revealed low awareness of chronic kidney disease (CKD) preventive practices (43.4%) among non-medical female university students in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia. In contrast, a Brazilian study [26] reported significantly higher knowledge levels (91.78%) regarding CKD prevention. The disparity in findings may reflect differences in sample size, with the Brazilian study involving a larger participant cohort."
}

