  "text": "Several explanations may account for these significant associations. Universities differ in the number and scope of the educational programs they offer, and institutions that include a medical college are likely to expose their students to more health-related content; such differences may plausibly explain why the university attended was associated with CKD knowledge. Similarly, the association with academic year may reflect greater exposure of some age groups to social media, which conveys a large volume of health information, or the fact that particular student cohorts had the opportunity to conduct awareness campaigns."
